{{Term/Store|Endura Carrot|Endura Carrots|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Endura Carrot}}
Endura Carrots are found at [[Malanya Spring]], near the peak of [[Satori Mountain]], and at the edges of [[Great Fairy Fountain]]s. Eating an Endura Carrot will heal [[Link]] for two [[Heart]]s. Endura Carrots can also be roasted by a [[Fire]] to make [[Roasted Endura Carrot]]s. They can also be [[Cooking|Cooked]] into a [[Meal]] using a [[Cooking Pot]] to temporarily grant Link [[Extra Stamina]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/>

Like [[Apple]]s and [[Swift Carrot]]s, Endura Carrots can be fed to [[Horse]]s to increase their [[Bond]]. Unlike other [[Food]]s that Horses can eat, Endura Carrots will temporarily increase the Horse's number of speed boosts granting them three extra yellow speed boosts which have a carrot icon next to them. After using up normal speed boosts and any granted by the [[Ancient Bridle]], these extra speed boosts can be used. However, they are lost afterwards. Roasted Endura Carrots have the same effect if eaten off the ground by a Horse. If the [[Giant Horse]] eats an Endura Carrot, only its Bond will be increased, as it has no speed boosts.

An Endura Carrot is required to revive a Horse via the Horse God, [[Malanya]].<ref name="BotW Malanya"/><ref name="BotW Malanya 2"/> If Link decides to give him an Endura Carrot, Malanya will agree to revive one of his Horses.<ref name="BotW Malanya 3"/> Endura Carrots can also be used at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] as an ingredient for [[Light Yellow Dye]]. Endura Carrots are not required to upgrade any pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].

